1
00:00:03,718 --> 00:00:05,690
<i>Number one
K-content channel.</i>

2
00:00:05,771 --> 00:00:07,685
<i>tvN for joy.</i>

3
00:00:09,005 --> 00:00:10,244
{\an8}<i>Fifteen.</i>

4
00:00:10,324 --> 00:00:11,464
{\an8}THE FOLLOWING PROGRAM IS
NOT SUITABLE FOR VIEWERS UNDER 15.

5
00:00:11,545 --> 00:00:12,712
{\an8}VIEWER DISCRETION IS ADVISED.

6
00:00:12,793 --> 00:00:13,894
{\an8}THIS PROGRAM CONTAINS PRODUCT PLACEMENTS
AND VIRTUAL ADVERTISING.

7
00:00:46,466 --> 00:00:49,886
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

8
00:00:49,966 --> 00:00:50,898
PRODUCTION SUPPORTED BY:
MINISTRY OF CULTURE, SPORTS AND TOURISM

9
00:00:50,978 --> 00:00:51,891
KOREA CREATIVE CONTENT AGENCY

10
00:00:51,971 --> 00:00:52,867
THIS DRAMA
IS A WORK OF FICTION

11
00:00:52,947 --> 00:00:53,900
CHILD AND ANIMAL SCENES WERE FILMED SAFELY
UNDER EXPERT SUPERVISION

12
00:01:02,563 --> 00:01:05,316
There's quite a competition
to launch their brand with us.

13
00:01:05,608 --> 00:01:07,276
There are over 30 brands

14
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,986
that have sent us samples
just this week.

15
00:01:09,570 --> 00:01:12,615
Many of these are dupes of what I saw
at the last Paris Fashion Week.

16
00:01:12,990 --> 00:01:15,243
It had many innovative designs

17
00:01:15,326 --> 00:01:17,620
so it looks like domestic brands
were heavily influenced.

18
00:01:17,703 --> 00:01:19,956
If all they can do is copy

19
00:01:20,039 --> 00:01:21,749
they can't work with Appello.

20
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:24,210
I'll look into just this brand.

21
00:01:24,961 --> 00:01:27,547
All right.
Ms. Seo, please help out with that.

22
00:01:27,630 --> 00:01:29,715
I'll join you right away
after figuring out the display.

23
00:01:29,799 --> 00:01:32,885
Yes, I'll get the models ready
for the fitting.

24
00:01:32,969 --> 00:01:34,512
- Okay, tell me when they're ready.
- Yes, sir.

25
00:01:37,848 --> 00:01:38,891
This is just like you.

26
00:01:39,684 --> 00:01:41,435
They aren't generic

27
00:01:42,687 --> 00:01:44,355
and they carry their own identity.

28
00:01:44,438 --> 00:01:46,190
That's how Appello started.

29
00:01:46,274 --> 00:01:48,234
I was just collecting the clothes
I wanted to wear

30
00:01:48,317 --> 00:01:49,777
which turned
into a tiny curated boutique.

31
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:53,364
And now, it's a platform
that carries hundreds of brands.

32
00:01:53,990 --> 00:01:55,533
The pressure is different now.

33
00:01:56,075 --> 00:01:58,077
Which you're carrying very well.

34
00:01:58,160 --> 00:01:59,203
I'm in charge of the direction.

35
00:01:59,620 --> 00:02:02,415
And if that direction is too skewed,
everyone who's following will fall.

36
00:02:02,707 --> 00:02:04,333
Gosh, I know

37
00:02:04,417 --> 00:02:05,918
that this is the time
to be more inclusive.

38
00:02:10,006 --> 00:02:11,090
Yes, sir.

39
00:02:12,383 --> 00:02:15,678
Yes, Mr. Kang. I'll do as you say
and pick up more mainstream designs.

40
00:02:20,266 --> 00:02:22,351
{\an8}EPISODE 2

41
00:02:24,729 --> 00:02:25,980
{\an8}Okay.

42
00:02:26,063 --> 00:02:28,190
{\an8}That bracelet on the man's hand.

43
00:02:28,274 --> 00:02:29,483
{\an8}- Take note of it.
- Yes.

44
00:02:32,236 --> 00:02:35,031
{\an8}Please get a tie
that's as bright as this one.

45
00:02:35,114 --> 00:02:36,616
{\an8}Right. Yes, sir.

46
00:02:37,658 --> 00:02:38,743
{\an8}Great work, everyone.

47
00:02:39,368 --> 00:02:40,411
{\an8}- Yes.
- Goodbye.

48
00:02:40,494 --> 00:02:42,121
{\an8}Text me the pictures we took today.

49
00:02:42,204 --> 00:02:45,458
{\an8}- Okay. Goodbye, Mr. Lee.
- Okay.

50
00:03:07,355 --> 00:03:10,650
<i>D.N.X! D.N.X! We love you, D.N.X!</i>

51
00:03:30,628 --> 00:03:32,880
You dropped this.

52
00:03:41,597 --> 00:03:43,516
Right. Thank you.

53
00:03:48,354 --> 00:03:49,355
Getting in?

54
00:03:50,606 --> 00:03:51,607
What?

55
00:03:53,317 --> 00:03:55,486
Oh, I am.

56
00:04:11,627 --> 00:04:12,920
<i>Don't be so nervous, Da-reum.</i>

57
00:04:13,003 --> 00:04:15,131
<i>Try to act as naturally as possible.</i>

58
00:04:22,054 --> 00:04:23,180
NAM DA-REUM

59
00:04:24,390 --> 00:04:26,142
- You must be one of the new hires.
- Sorry?

60
00:04:31,188 --> 00:04:32,189
Yes.

61
00:04:32,773 --> 00:04:34,066
Why weren't you there
at the welcome dinner?

62
00:04:37,528 --> 00:04:39,739
I got a bit drunk last night

63
00:04:40,573 --> 00:04:41,866
and went home early.

64
00:04:42,908 --> 00:04:44,702
I see.

65
00:04:46,829 --> 00:04:48,789
Anyway, it's nice to meet you,
Da-reum.

66
00:04:53,377 --> 00:04:54,837
How do you know my name?

67
00:04:56,589 --> 00:04:57,757
I look forward to working with you.

68
00:05:12,104 --> 00:05:13,522
I'll do my best.

69
00:05:17,109 --> 00:05:18,110
See you around.

70
00:05:20,154 --> 00:05:21,489
Yes, Mr. Lee.

71
00:05:28,662 --> 00:05:29,872
Goodbye.

72
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:52,186
My gosh.

73
00:05:53,521 --> 00:05:55,189
My gosh!

74
00:05:55,272 --> 00:05:58,943
I shook hands with Chan!

75
00:06:01,111 --> 00:06:02,780
My gosh!

76
00:06:05,658 --> 00:06:07,910
Great job on not getting too nervous.

77
00:06:07,993 --> 00:06:09,537
Good one, Da-reum.

78
00:06:23,759 --> 00:06:24,927
Goodbye.

79
00:06:32,935 --> 00:06:37,231
WOLHWA SILVER WORKSHOP

80
00:06:49,785 --> 00:06:53,372
Hey, what have you been
doing here for days?

81
00:06:54,331 --> 00:06:56,041
Are you looking for a career change?

82
00:06:56,333 --> 00:06:57,501
Should I do that?

83
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:00,629
D.N.X has disbanded

84
00:07:00,713 --> 00:07:02,715
and not many would remember Lee Chan.

85
00:07:04,383 --> 00:07:05,384
Hey.

86
00:07:05,926 --> 00:07:07,011
I'm pretty good, aren't I?

87
00:07:07,845 --> 00:07:10,347
You might as well
open a jewelry studio.

88
00:07:13,559 --> 00:07:16,770
Hey, clean up everything
before I come back.

89
00:07:16,854 --> 00:07:17,855
Okay?

90
00:07:18,355 --> 00:07:19,481
Okay?

91
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:48,344
- Hello.
- Hello.

92
00:07:48,427 --> 00:07:50,471
By any chance, how much is this?

93
00:07:50,930 --> 00:07:54,433
This is a DIY jewelry studio,
so we do not sell any items.

94
00:07:54,516 --> 00:07:56,977
This was
one of our customers' designs.

95
00:07:57,311 --> 00:08:01,482
This is the exact shape
that my all-time favorite celebrity

96
00:08:01,565 --> 00:08:03,567
always draws
when he signs autographs.

97
00:08:04,443 --> 00:08:05,945
Today's my birthday

98
00:08:06,028 --> 00:08:08,238
so I want to buy it for myself
as a gift.

99
00:08:08,322 --> 00:08:09,782
Can I please buy it?

100
00:08:10,824 --> 00:08:12,242
I'm sorry.

101
00:08:12,326 --> 00:08:14,620
But why don't you
try making it yourself?

102
00:08:16,413 --> 00:08:19,416
I don't think
I can make it look exactly the same.

103
00:08:19,500 --> 00:08:23,253
It's not as difficult as you think.

104
00:08:25,547 --> 00:08:26,799
It's okay.

105
00:08:27,549 --> 00:08:29,843
I understand. Thank you.

106
00:08:29,927 --> 00:08:31,553
- Sure.
- Goodbye.

107
00:08:31,637 --> 00:08:32,846
Okay. Goodbye.

108
00:08:36,100 --> 00:08:39,228
WOLHWA SILVER WORKSHOP

109
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:57,371
It was you from back then.

110
00:09:02,084 --> 00:09:04,920
- Great work today.
- Goodbye!

111
00:09:05,879 --> 00:09:09,216
We've all done so well today!
See you tomorrow.

112
00:09:09,591 --> 00:09:12,302
See you tomorrow! Bye!

113
00:09:13,762 --> 00:09:17,850
It looks like something great
must've happened to Da-reum.

114
00:09:17,933 --> 00:09:20,728
Right? Our team has been
swamped with work lately.

115
00:09:21,061 --> 00:09:24,148
Min-a, if it's okay with you

116
00:09:24,231 --> 00:09:25,941
why don't we grab a glass of beer?

117
00:09:26,025 --> 00:09:28,068
Gosh, beer?

118
00:09:28,986 --> 00:09:30,070
No.

119
00:09:32,114 --> 00:09:33,157
No?

120
00:09:39,747 --> 00:09:41,248
<i>You must be one of the new hires.</i>

121
00:09:48,338 --> 00:09:49,506
SUNGJU STATION

122
00:09:53,385 --> 00:09:54,553
<i>It's nice to meet you, Da-reum.</i>

123
00:09:56,472 --> 00:09:59,433
It was so great to meet you.

124
00:10:05,022 --> 00:10:06,273
<i>See you around.</i>

125
00:10:19,328 --> 00:10:21,080
See you!

126
00:10:21,163 --> 00:10:23,499
Chan, let us meet again!

127
00:10:23,582 --> 00:10:25,000
See you, Da-reum!

128
00:10:26,376 --> 00:10:27,503
Bye!

129
00:10:32,216 --> 00:10:33,467
Are you that happy?

130
00:10:35,010 --> 00:10:36,011
Yes.

131
00:10:36,553 --> 00:10:38,722
Someone might think
you just won the lottery.

132
00:10:38,806 --> 00:10:40,432
It's her ultimate fan moment.

133
00:10:40,516 --> 00:10:43,143
Fans who lived outside Seoul
can't go to music show recordings.

134
00:10:43,227 --> 00:10:47,815
And at concerts, they look this small
so you can't even see their faces.

135
00:10:48,357 --> 00:10:50,776
You've made it, Namda.

136
00:10:50,859 --> 00:10:53,654
So? Would you like to smell my hand?

137
00:10:53,737 --> 00:10:55,239
Jeez.

138
00:10:55,322 --> 00:10:56,990
- No!
- Me too!

139
00:10:57,074 --> 00:11:00,077
No, it's going to wear off.
I can't lose it!

140
00:11:02,496 --> 00:11:04,832
Today is the first time
I've seen Chan in person.

141
00:11:05,958 --> 00:11:08,544
I'll always celebrate this day.

142
00:11:08,627 --> 00:11:11,380
You've always insisted
Chan gave you that necklace.

143
00:11:11,713 --> 00:11:13,632
Do you finally admit
that you were overly hopeful?

144
00:11:19,346 --> 00:11:23,934
But no one else
could have possibly made this.

145
00:11:35,988 --> 00:11:37,114
Excuse me.

146
00:11:42,286 --> 00:11:43,287
Happy birthday.

147
00:12:17,946 --> 00:12:20,866
He definitely sounded like him too.

148
00:12:20,949 --> 00:12:23,994
You're just misremembering
as a hopeful fan.

149
00:12:25,621 --> 00:12:26,788
You think so?

150
00:12:27,039 --> 00:12:28,207
Well, anyway.

151
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:32,044
I finally met him in person. My gosh!

152
00:12:32,127 --> 00:12:33,795
I'm not dreaming, am I?

153
00:12:35,714 --> 00:12:37,090
It hurts!

154
00:12:37,174 --> 00:12:38,217
- It's not.
- It hurts.

155
00:12:38,300 --> 00:12:40,010
APPELLO

156
00:12:42,179 --> 00:12:44,181
This time, the overseas training
for outstanding employees

157
00:12:44,264 --> 00:12:46,183
will be held
at the New York Fashion Week.

158
00:12:46,558 --> 00:12:47,559
New York?

159
00:12:47,935 --> 00:12:49,186
It sounds perfect.

160
00:12:49,603 --> 00:12:51,146
You'll get to see a lot

161
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:54,608
and also have a mountain of work.

162
00:12:55,150 --> 00:12:57,569
Overseas training
for outstanding employees?

163
00:12:58,070 --> 00:13:00,405
It's a tradition of sorts
that Director Lee has made

164
00:13:00,489 --> 00:13:02,908
since the foundation of Appello.

165
00:13:02,991 --> 00:13:04,701
Once a year,
we pick out an outstanding employee

166
00:13:04,785 --> 00:13:06,161
to do a project abroad.

167
00:13:06,828 --> 00:13:09,623
Someone will be chosen
early next year.

168
00:13:11,041 --> 00:13:13,085
Thank you. Come here, Min-a.

169
00:13:14,086 --> 00:13:15,420
Does that mean

170
00:13:15,796 --> 00:13:17,714
Director Lee will go on the trip too?

171
00:13:17,798 --> 00:13:18,882
Of course.

172
00:13:19,341 --> 00:13:21,635
He has never missed it once.

173
00:13:21,718 --> 00:13:23,595
Who picks out
the outstanding employee?

174
00:13:23,679 --> 00:13:24,680
Mr. Kang.

175
00:13:27,766 --> 00:13:29,059
Mr. Kang?

176
00:13:40,779 --> 00:13:42,030
AVOID MR. KANG

177
00:13:42,447 --> 00:13:43,448
WORK HARD!

178
00:13:47,619 --> 00:13:49,454
{\an8}EMPLOYEE OVERSEAS TRAINING!
GET ON MR. KANG'S GOOD SIDE!

179
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:54,209
Well...

180
00:13:55,002 --> 00:13:58,755
Is it okay
for my goal to change so drastically?

181
00:13:59,923 --> 00:14:02,134
No, Da-reum.

182
00:14:02,676 --> 00:14:04,428
You can do this.

183
00:14:07,097 --> 00:14:08,181
First of all

184
00:14:09,516 --> 00:14:13,186
I must figure out
what Mr. Kang is like.

185
00:14:16,898 --> 00:14:19,151
Ms. Kim, this is for you.

186
00:14:19,234 --> 00:14:20,360
Thank you.

187
00:14:22,070 --> 00:14:23,780
Ms. Kim.

188
00:14:24,114 --> 00:14:26,742
So what does Mr. Kang like?

189
00:14:27,492 --> 00:14:28,535
Why are you asking about him?

190
00:14:30,537 --> 00:14:34,541
I wasn't exactly
on my best behavior since day one

191
00:14:35,083 --> 00:14:36,710
so I wanted to improve my reputation

192
00:14:36,793 --> 00:14:38,587
and do my best at work.

193
00:14:39,629 --> 00:14:40,672
Is that so?

194
00:14:41,214 --> 00:14:42,758
Mr. Kang...

195
00:14:44,801 --> 00:14:48,180
He only uses the brown capsules
for the coffee machine.

196
00:14:51,725 --> 00:14:52,851
The brown ones?

197
00:14:53,810 --> 00:14:55,020
<i>Chocolate latte.</i>

198
00:14:55,103 --> 00:14:56,938
<i>He has a sweet tooth,
unlike how he seems.</i>

199
00:14:57,981 --> 00:14:59,733
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
OFFER HIM CHOCOLATE LATTE

200
00:15:06,865 --> 00:15:08,492
Mr. Kang.

201
00:15:08,575 --> 00:15:10,869
Would you like
a cup of sweet chocolate latte?

202
00:15:10,952 --> 00:15:12,120
I made it just now.

203
00:15:15,499 --> 00:15:18,293
No, I only drink one cup a day
because of my blood glucose level.

204
00:15:18,377 --> 00:15:20,462
I've already had it,
so enjoy it for yourself.

205
00:15:25,634 --> 00:15:26,635
Okay.

206
00:15:26,718 --> 00:15:28,553
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT CHOCOLATE LATTE

207
00:15:30,097 --> 00:15:33,767
<i>I think he spends time on the rooftop
right after eating lunch.</i>

208
00:15:33,850 --> 00:15:36,645
<i>He likes to spend at least 20 minutes
a day in the sun.</i>

209
00:15:36,728 --> 00:15:38,063
{\an8}GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
BE SUNLIGHT BUDDIES

210
00:15:45,737 --> 00:15:49,658
Oh, my.
I didn't know you came here too.

211
00:15:49,783 --> 00:15:51,368
Great view, isn't it?

212
00:15:51,451 --> 00:15:52,494
Yes.

213
00:15:53,870 --> 00:15:56,915
I always get my share of sunlight

214
00:15:56,998 --> 00:15:58,834
whenever I'm done with lunch.

215
00:15:58,917 --> 00:16:01,461
People need sunlight to stay healthy.

216
00:16:01,837 --> 00:16:05,424
Mr. Kang, people these days
are often low on vitamin D.

217
00:16:05,507 --> 00:16:07,134
- Ms. Nam.
- Yes?

218
00:16:12,931 --> 00:16:15,100
You're very distracting.
And don't stand in my view.

219
00:16:18,145 --> 00:16:19,146
Right.

220
00:16:19,563 --> 00:16:20,730
I'm sorry.

221
00:16:23,108 --> 00:16:24,901
GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT SUNLIGHT BUDDIES

222
00:16:26,111 --> 00:16:29,030
<i>Also, when you compliment him
on his style</i>

223
00:16:29,114 --> 00:16:30,490
<i>he gets somewhat pleased.</i>

224
00:16:30,574 --> 00:16:32,075
{\an8}GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
COMPLIMENT HIM

225
00:16:33,201 --> 00:16:35,704
My gosh, Mr. Kang.

226
00:16:35,787 --> 00:16:39,458
You look so cool
in that shirt and tie.

227
00:16:39,541 --> 00:16:40,959
You could be a runway model.

228
00:16:41,042 --> 00:16:43,044
I pulled an all-nighter,
so it's the same as yesterday.

229
00:16:47,841 --> 00:16:49,092
Goodbye.

230
00:16:52,387 --> 00:16:53,722
{\an8}GUIDE TO WINNING CEO KANG HA-GI
CROSS OUT COMPLIMENTS

231
00:16:53,805 --> 00:16:56,016
{\an8}How come nothing is working?

232
00:17:05,734 --> 00:17:09,029
<i>You look so cool
in that shirt and tie.</i>

233
00:17:09,446 --> 00:17:10,864
You could be a runway model.

234
00:17:18,330 --> 00:17:19,414
My gosh.

235
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:27,881
I looked into Ms. Nam

236
00:17:27,964 --> 00:17:29,633
and she recently quit...

237
00:17:29,716 --> 00:17:31,968
Just speak normally.
It's just the two of us here.

238
00:17:32,427 --> 00:17:33,428
Yes, sir.

239
00:17:33,512 --> 00:17:36,932
Ms. Nam recently resigned
from her job at SE Corporation.

240
00:17:38,725 --> 00:17:42,229
I feel like she has a hidden agenda.

241
00:17:42,521 --> 00:17:44,606
Maybe she's a honey trap

242
00:17:44,689 --> 00:17:45,732
sent by Director Kim.

243
00:17:47,734 --> 00:17:48,777
Honey trap?

244
00:17:49,653 --> 00:17:50,654
I don't think so.

245
00:17:50,737 --> 00:17:52,280
Exactly. It's nonsense.

246
00:17:53,448 --> 00:17:55,992
How about a cuteness ploy?
Someone who traps you with cuteness.

247
00:17:59,621 --> 00:18:00,830
That also doesn't make sense.

248
00:18:01,206 --> 00:18:02,624
Is she here just to wreak havoc?

249
00:18:13,134 --> 00:18:16,137
How do I get on Mr. Kang's good side?

250
00:18:16,721 --> 00:18:18,431
- What's up?
- I mean

251
00:18:18,932 --> 00:18:22,435
whenever I say something,
all he says is, "No, thanks."

252
00:18:22,519 --> 00:18:25,355
There's no way to get through to him.

253
00:18:25,438 --> 00:18:27,190
It's not like I'm into him.

254
00:18:27,274 --> 00:18:28,775
I'm trying to be
the outstanding employee.

255
00:18:28,858 --> 00:18:31,152
Maybe he thinks
you're hitting on him.

256
00:18:31,236 --> 00:18:34,030
He just doesn't let anyone
get close to him.

257
00:18:34,114 --> 00:18:35,865
Is that why he shuts you off?

258
00:18:36,408 --> 00:18:38,493
No, he's like that
to everyone else too.

259
00:18:38,577 --> 00:18:40,245
That's why the employees

260
00:18:40,328 --> 00:18:42,581
nicknamed him Icy Kang.

261
00:18:42,664 --> 00:18:43,957
He's that cold.

262
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,585
Hey, look at this.

263
00:18:46,668 --> 00:18:49,296
<i>Exclusive! Former K-pop idol
and top actor A is allegedly gay.</i>

264
00:18:49,379 --> 00:18:51,381
<i>The boyfriend, B, is the current CEO
of his fashion platform.</i>

265
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:53,466
<i>Rumors say he hired him
to keep their relationship secret.</i>

266
00:18:53,550 --> 00:18:55,093
<i>No way. That's obviously Appello.</i>

267
00:18:55,176 --> 00:18:56,177
<i>Totes. It's Appello.</i>

268
00:18:56,261 --> 00:18:58,054
<i>Wow, Lee Chan is gay?</i>

269
00:18:58,138 --> 00:19:00,390
<i>- He's gay?
- He's gay?</i>

270
00:19:01,141 --> 00:19:04,894
Hey, are A and B here referring

271
00:19:05,186 --> 00:19:06,855
- to Chan and your CEO?
- What?

272
00:19:07,439 --> 00:19:08,440
What?

273
00:19:08,815 --> 00:19:09,816
Are they dating?

274
00:19:10,442 --> 00:19:11,943
What are you talking about?

275
00:19:12,485 --> 00:19:13,570
Chan is...

276
00:19:15,363 --> 00:19:16,615
a heterosexual.

277
00:19:16,698 --> 00:19:19,200
He once said in an interview
that an older girl at his high school

278
00:19:19,284 --> 00:19:20,577
was his first love.

279
00:19:21,119 --> 00:19:22,120
Then what is this?

280
00:19:22,203 --> 00:19:24,831
What do you think? A blind item
circulating in the financial world.

281
00:19:25,624 --> 00:19:28,084
Our company CEO and Chan?

282
00:19:28,585 --> 00:19:29,836
No way.

283
00:19:35,425 --> 00:19:36,760
No, impossible.

284
00:20:20,220 --> 00:20:21,763
Oh, come on.

285
00:20:30,105 --> 00:20:31,731
Hey, get up and eat.

286
00:20:46,162 --> 00:20:47,872
Yes, this is what I'm talking about.

287
00:20:48,415 --> 00:20:49,999
Wait, aren't you eating?

288
00:20:50,667 --> 00:20:52,043
This is how I eat breakfast.

289
00:20:53,420 --> 00:20:56,673
Hey, grabbing a drink was an excuse.
You came to eat that, right?

290
00:20:57,674 --> 00:20:58,675
Bingo.

291
00:21:03,054 --> 00:21:05,765
Gosh, yes. That hits the spot.

292
00:21:05,849 --> 00:21:07,851
It tastes just like your mother's...

293
00:21:18,820 --> 00:21:21,281
Gosh, it's so filling
to finally eat a home-cooked meal.

294
00:21:22,031 --> 00:21:23,408
Can I stay at your place for a while?

295
00:21:23,491 --> 00:21:26,369
No, I had to sleep on the couch,
and my back is killing me.

296
00:21:26,453 --> 00:21:27,579
We could've shared the bed.

297
00:21:29,372 --> 00:21:30,373
Are you insane?

298
00:21:31,374 --> 00:21:32,625
I'm running late.

299
00:21:32,709 --> 00:21:33,960
Eat, clean up, and go.

300
00:21:35,044 --> 00:21:36,045
Hey.

301
00:21:36,921 --> 00:21:38,965
Take this. You haven't even eaten.

302
00:21:39,549 --> 00:21:41,926
- What's this?
- I got it from someone I work with.

303
00:21:42,510 --> 00:21:43,970
It should be good.
If anything, they know good food.

304
00:21:44,721 --> 00:21:45,764
Take it.

305
00:21:48,266 --> 00:21:49,684
- Bye.
- Bye.

306
00:21:49,768 --> 00:21:50,852
Clean up before you go!

307
00:21:54,856 --> 00:21:56,191
CEO KANG HA-GI

308
00:23:02,465 --> 00:23:03,466
Come in.

309
00:23:03,883 --> 00:23:06,427
Mr. Kang, the weekly meeting
for the marketing team is ready.

310
00:23:06,511 --> 00:23:08,304
- Okay. I'll be there.
- Yes, sir.

311
00:23:28,157 --> 00:23:29,409
Jeez.

312
00:23:34,372 --> 00:23:36,958
Hey, come and take these now.

313
00:23:37,041 --> 00:23:39,586
Yes, for this lookbook shooting

314
00:23:39,669 --> 00:23:42,505
we want to focus on gorpcore

315
00:23:42,589 --> 00:23:45,592
as that is the trending aesthetic
at the moment.

316
00:23:52,599 --> 00:23:54,809
Hobbies that are on the rise

317
00:23:54,893 --> 00:23:58,354
include hiking, tennis, and running.

318
00:23:58,730 --> 00:24:02,317
But the outfits
for these hobbies look too sporty.

319
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:03,401
So?

320
00:24:03,902 --> 00:24:04,903
What's your point?

321
00:24:06,613 --> 00:24:08,114
- Sorry?
- The key point.

322
00:24:09,157 --> 00:24:10,158
The key point...

323
00:24:16,122 --> 00:24:19,042
The visual concept
for the next season

324
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:21,044
is camping.

325
00:24:22,837 --> 00:24:23,963
Okay, camping.

326
00:24:24,756 --> 00:24:25,924
Sounds great.

327
00:24:26,007 --> 00:24:27,133
From now on

328
00:24:28,009 --> 00:24:30,637
please do not spend
over a minute on your presentation.

329
00:24:31,095 --> 00:24:32,889
I'm not looking for

330
00:24:32,972 --> 00:24:36,142
an elaborate speech,
but the actual result of your work.

331
00:24:38,061 --> 00:24:39,228
Yes, sir.

332
00:24:39,687 --> 00:24:40,939
Are we done here?

333
00:24:41,439 --> 00:24:43,483
- Yes.
- This week

334
00:24:43,900 --> 00:24:45,860
I expect everyone to go all-in
on the Appello fashion show.

335
00:24:46,361 --> 00:24:47,987
It would be nice to film
what the venue is like

336
00:24:48,071 --> 00:24:49,906
and upload it to our official
social media accounts.

337
00:24:49,989 --> 00:24:50,990
Any volunteers?

338
00:24:55,745 --> 00:24:59,415
<i>Lastly, Mr. Kang likes
those who take the initiative.</i>

339
00:24:59,499 --> 00:25:01,709
<i>Someone who steps up
and tries to make things happen.</i>

340
00:25:02,168 --> 00:25:03,252
I will

341
00:25:03,753 --> 00:25:04,754
do it.

342
00:25:07,006 --> 00:25:09,801
Other people have a lot of work to do

343
00:25:09,884 --> 00:25:11,302
so I'll do it.

344
00:25:11,803 --> 00:25:13,471
Yes, she has been assisting

345
00:25:13,554 --> 00:25:15,807
with the management
of our social media account

346
00:25:15,890 --> 00:25:17,100
so it'll help.

347
00:25:21,646 --> 00:25:22,647
All right, then.

348
00:25:24,899 --> 00:25:26,317
We'll go and see the rehearsal today

349
00:25:26,776 --> 00:25:28,736
so be at my office by two o'clock.

350
00:25:28,820 --> 00:25:29,821
Yes, sir.

351
00:25:30,697 --> 00:25:32,281
Hey, Da-reum.

352
00:25:32,699 --> 00:25:35,576
It's your first time on site.
Are you sure you'll be fine?

353
00:25:37,286 --> 00:25:38,496
Mr. Kang.

354
00:25:39,831 --> 00:25:42,083
I think I should probably go.

355
00:25:42,166 --> 00:25:43,376
Let's give the volunteer a try.

356
00:25:46,254 --> 00:25:47,255
That's all, then.

357
00:25:47,338 --> 00:25:48,423
- Yes.
- Yes.

358
00:25:50,925 --> 00:25:51,926
Good luck.

359
00:26:17,201 --> 00:26:18,244
Mr. Kang...

360
00:26:35,636 --> 00:26:37,096
Everything is so neatly organized

361
00:26:38,056 --> 00:26:39,766
as expected from the office's owner.

362
00:26:41,893 --> 00:26:43,728
I can't believe I spent a night here.

363
00:26:55,698 --> 00:26:58,326
I want to be an outstanding employee
to join this trip.

364
00:27:06,459 --> 00:27:08,086
Wait, what?

365
00:27:09,378 --> 00:27:11,297
Why is he

366
00:27:11,923 --> 00:27:13,257
looking at him like that?

367
00:27:36,447 --> 00:27:37,698
<i>What can I do</i>

368
00:27:38,199 --> 00:27:40,284
<i>to show you how I feel?</i>

369
00:27:41,119 --> 00:27:43,204
<i>I love you, Chan.</i>

370
00:27:43,538 --> 00:27:46,833
<i>- I love you, Chan.</i>
- "I love you, Chan"?

371
00:28:10,982 --> 00:28:12,233
<i>What can I do</i>

372
00:28:13,151 --> 00:28:15,111
<i>to show you how I feel?</i>

373
00:28:17,238 --> 00:28:18,239
<i>I love you...</i>

374
00:28:20,533 --> 00:28:21,701
<i>Chan.</i>

375
00:28:29,750 --> 00:28:31,127
That blind item

376
00:28:32,420 --> 00:28:33,713
must be true.

377
00:28:36,382 --> 00:28:38,134
What do I do? What now?

378
00:28:50,188 --> 00:28:51,522
NO IMPORTANT DOCUMENT ON THE DESK

379
00:28:51,856 --> 00:28:53,649
- Did you wait long?
- Sorry?

380
00:28:54,317 --> 00:28:55,484
No, I just got here.

381
00:28:55,568 --> 00:28:59,655
I left the weekly meeting report
on your desk, sir.

382
00:29:11,500 --> 00:29:12,668
NO LEAKAGE OF CONFIDENTIAL INFO

383
00:29:19,091 --> 00:29:20,259
- Let's go.
- Sorry?

384
00:29:20,343 --> 00:29:22,261
Right. Yes.

385
00:29:22,845 --> 00:29:23,846
Let's go.

386
00:29:38,342 --> 00:29:39,343
- These days,
- Yes?

387
00:29:42,555 --> 00:29:44,265
is the job market tough?

388
00:29:46,642 --> 00:29:49,937
Yes, that's the case.

389
00:29:51,189 --> 00:29:53,941
Someone with your credentials
could've gone to major corporations.

390
00:29:54,025 --> 00:29:55,026
Gosh, hardly.

391
00:29:55,985 --> 00:29:57,069
By any chance

392
00:29:58,154 --> 00:30:00,239
any special reason
why you came to Appello?

393
00:30:03,659 --> 00:30:06,871
Actually, I wanted
to learn more about myself.

394
00:30:07,330 --> 00:30:08,915
Instead of just getting
more qualifications

395
00:30:08,998 --> 00:30:11,918
I wanted to find out
what I truly love.

396
00:30:12,168 --> 00:30:15,379
That was why I chose
to come to a place I was drawn to.

397
00:30:16,714 --> 00:30:17,757
Also

398
00:30:18,716 --> 00:30:22,053
there was someone
I really wanted to meet.

399
00:30:24,513 --> 00:30:25,681
Who is it?

400
00:30:27,350 --> 00:30:28,351
What?

401
00:30:30,478 --> 00:30:31,687
Did I just say it out loud?

402
00:30:31,771 --> 00:30:33,189
That was why I heard it.

403
00:30:38,361 --> 00:30:40,029
Well, what I meant

404
00:30:40,905 --> 00:30:44,283
was that I wanted to meet many people
in different industries on the job.

405
00:30:44,367 --> 00:30:45,743
Something like that.

406
00:30:49,997 --> 00:30:53,209
Mr. Kang, may I ask something too?

407
00:30:54,543 --> 00:30:55,544
Sure.

408
00:30:55,878 --> 00:30:58,714
Why did you come to Appello?

409
00:31:03,344 --> 00:31:06,180
At first,
it was because of one person.

410
00:31:06,931 --> 00:31:09,850
<i>Could that be Chan?</i>

411
00:31:09,934 --> 00:31:12,812
But now, Appello is my everything.

412
00:31:45,761 --> 00:31:47,596
- What's this? A prize draw?
- It's a prize draw.

413
00:31:47,680 --> 00:31:48,681
Thank you.

414
00:31:53,311 --> 00:31:54,437
My gosh. So that's how it looks.

415
00:31:56,230 --> 00:31:57,315
That's cool.

416
00:32:06,282 --> 00:32:07,783
That is so awesome.

417
00:32:09,327 --> 00:32:11,203
Is she putting on a show,
trying to look innocent?

418
00:32:12,747 --> 00:32:14,498
Goodness, Mr. Kang!

419
00:32:15,207 --> 00:32:18,252
I can't believe
you came all the way here yourself.

420
00:32:18,919 --> 00:32:20,713
- Hello.
- Of course, I should come.

421
00:32:20,963 --> 00:32:22,089
How's it coming along?

422
00:32:22,173 --> 00:32:23,341
Yes, of course.

423
00:32:23,924 --> 00:32:26,135
A new brand like ours
could never even dream

424
00:32:26,218 --> 00:32:27,345
of having a fashion show.

425
00:32:27,428 --> 00:32:29,889
Thank you very much
for giving us this great opportunity.

426
00:32:30,097 --> 00:32:32,725
Don't mention it.
Your brand already had the appeal.

427
00:32:32,808 --> 00:32:33,851
The opportunity simply found you.

428
00:32:35,353 --> 00:32:37,605
Anyway, I've never seen those before.

429
00:32:38,981 --> 00:32:41,942
This kind of event is a rare chance.

430
00:32:43,194 --> 00:32:46,864
So we even took out a loan
to make lots of new products.

431
00:32:47,782 --> 00:32:49,450
Although we wouldn't survive

432
00:32:49,533 --> 00:32:51,619
until the next season
if they end up as inventory.

433
00:32:52,203 --> 00:32:54,163
Oh, I almost jinxed it. Never mind.

434
00:32:54,246 --> 00:32:55,539
I won't let that happen.

435
00:32:55,623 --> 00:32:57,875
I'll make sure

436
00:32:57,958 --> 00:33:01,504
people see our products
and immediately go, "It's Go.Co."

437
00:33:01,587 --> 00:33:03,130
I will make it happen.

438
00:33:03,214 --> 00:33:04,423
I can do it!

439
00:33:04,965 --> 00:33:06,801
- Yes, please keep up the good work.
- Thanks.

440
00:33:06,884 --> 00:33:07,885
See you at the show.

441
00:33:07,968 --> 00:33:10,179
All right. Keep it up, Mr. Kang!

442
00:33:10,513 --> 00:33:11,722
- Let's go!
- Go for it!

443
00:33:18,187 --> 00:33:19,188
What are you smiling about?

444
00:33:21,857 --> 00:33:24,402
I had a thought that fashion brands

445
00:33:24,485 --> 00:33:26,987
and K-pop idol groups are similar.

446
00:33:27,905 --> 00:33:29,448
- K-pop idol?
- Yes.

447
00:33:30,449 --> 00:33:32,535
They show their presence on the stage

448
00:33:32,618 --> 00:33:35,246
bring thrills to people
with their visuals

449
00:33:35,329 --> 00:33:37,998
and above all, they're loved
by their fans for a very long time.

450
00:33:42,670 --> 00:33:45,131
Everyone must've put in
so much hard work

451
00:33:45,214 --> 00:33:47,425
just to get their chance
on that stage.

452
00:33:49,635 --> 00:33:51,804
I really hope this fashion show

453
00:33:52,304 --> 00:33:53,722
becomes a huge hit.

454
00:33:54,849 --> 00:33:57,101
I'll put in everything I have too.

455
00:34:14,326 --> 00:34:16,620
Now, let us begin!

456
00:34:17,079 --> 00:34:19,248
The first model, walk up to the spot.

457
00:34:19,331 --> 00:34:21,667
Maintain a three-second interval.
Now, go!

458
00:34:39,018 --> 00:34:40,561
Cool.

459
00:34:51,155 --> 00:34:52,406
- What happened?
- Cut.

460
00:34:52,490 --> 00:34:53,616
Are you okay?

461
00:34:53,699 --> 00:34:56,619
- Hey, go check on the model.
- Yes, sir.

462
00:34:57,411 --> 00:34:59,497
Reduce the amount of dry ice.

463
00:35:00,539 --> 00:35:03,751
- Was it because of dry ice?
- Yes, it looks like it.

464
00:35:03,834 --> 00:35:05,961
If too much dry ice is used,
it creates vapors.

465
00:35:10,382 --> 00:35:13,844
That's why he almost fell
on stage before.

466
00:35:13,928 --> 00:35:15,471
Let's wipe the stage.

467
00:35:15,554 --> 00:35:17,181
Can I have someone test the stage
before we begin?

468
00:35:17,264 --> 00:35:19,016
Anyone wearing dress shoes
among the staff?

469
00:35:25,648 --> 00:35:26,649
Can I do it?

470
00:35:26,732 --> 00:35:29,151
These heels are pretty low.
I think these will be okay.

471
00:35:29,777 --> 00:35:32,863
- Can I ask you to do it then?
- Of course.

472
00:35:32,947 --> 00:35:34,615
Why would you?

473
00:35:34,698 --> 00:35:36,450
If models get hurt, that will cause
problems for the show.

474
00:35:36,534 --> 00:35:38,327
I'll go walk slowly.

475
00:35:38,410 --> 00:35:41,288
- Do I start behind the stage?
- Yes. Thank you.

476
00:36:00,266 --> 00:36:01,475
Oh, no.

477
00:36:08,732 --> 00:36:09,733
Ms. Nam!

478
00:36:35,801 --> 00:36:37,386
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

479
00:36:38,095 --> 00:36:39,805
Oh, yes. I'm okay.

480
00:36:40,639 --> 00:36:43,559
You should've just walked.
Why did you make a turn?

481
00:36:43,642 --> 00:36:45,603
You almost hurt your head
from your carelessness.

482
00:36:47,813 --> 00:36:49,732
I know. Why did I do that?

483
00:36:52,484 --> 00:36:54,612
It's a bit watery over here.

484
00:36:54,695 --> 00:36:57,281
Someone should wipe over here.

485
00:36:57,364 --> 00:36:59,783
- Okay. Hey, go wipe it.
- Yes.

486
00:37:07,291 --> 00:37:10,085
We have Lee Chan playing the role

487
00:37:10,169 --> 00:37:12,671
of Seong-jun who appears
to be perfect in every way

488
00:37:12,755 --> 00:37:14,632
but actually clumsy and vulnerable
when it comes to love

489
00:37:14,715 --> 00:37:19,303
and Yoon Cho-yi who plays the role
of Yi-seo who matures by experiencing

490
00:37:19,386 --> 00:37:21,221
the sweetest moment
as well as the most bitter breakup.

491
00:37:21,305 --> 00:37:24,016
The two lead roles of <i>Bitter Sweet</i>.
Can you please make a heart?

492
00:37:26,435 --> 00:37:27,853
Can you look to the left?

493
00:37:28,395 --> 00:37:29,438
Now, to the center.

494
00:37:29,897 --> 00:37:30,981
To the right, please.

495
00:37:31,732 --> 00:37:33,192
Very nice.

496
00:37:34,485 --> 00:37:36,153
It's time for questions.

497
00:37:36,236 --> 00:37:38,614
If you have any questions,
please raise your hands

498
00:37:38,697 --> 00:37:39,990
and we'll pass you the mic.

499
00:37:40,616 --> 00:37:42,284
- Yes?
- Your unique chemistry was

500
00:37:42,368 --> 00:37:44,578
already evident in the preview.

501
00:37:44,662 --> 00:37:46,330
I wonder if you grew any feelings
for each other

502
00:37:46,413 --> 00:37:49,041
while working on this film.

503
00:37:49,333 --> 00:37:53,504
Well, to be honest, who wouldn't be
fluttered to see Lee Chan?

504
00:37:54,129 --> 00:37:56,924
I've been a fan of his
for a long time

505
00:37:57,007 --> 00:37:59,802
so that helped me focus
on portraying my emotions.

506
00:38:02,388 --> 00:38:04,014
Well, Ms. Cho-yi is very lovely.

507
00:38:04,473 --> 00:38:06,600
I think this drama did a good job

508
00:38:06,684 --> 00:38:08,644
of showcasing her charms.

509
00:38:08,727 --> 00:38:11,980
If I meet someone like her
in real life

510
00:38:13,816 --> 00:38:15,651
I can't help but fall in love.

511
00:38:19,738 --> 00:38:22,491
LEE CHAN AND YOON CHO-YI
GETTING FLUTTERED WHILE FILMING?

512
00:38:24,076 --> 00:38:25,869
Good job today.

513
00:38:25,953 --> 00:38:27,371
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

514
00:38:27,454 --> 00:38:28,497
See you later.

515
00:38:28,580 --> 00:38:29,998
- Bye.
- Bye.

516
00:38:33,711 --> 00:38:35,421
Good work, Mr. Lee.

517
00:38:36,004 --> 00:38:37,256
Yes, good work.

518
00:38:43,595 --> 00:38:44,847
Give me a second.

519
00:38:51,812 --> 00:38:54,440
Did you receive the gift I sent you?

520
00:38:55,065 --> 00:38:56,525
I gave it to my friend.

521
00:38:56,942 --> 00:38:57,943
What?

522
00:39:00,028 --> 00:39:02,489
You've been ignoring my calls.
How long will you keep doing this?

523
00:39:02,906 --> 00:39:03,949
Cho-yi.

524
00:39:05,701 --> 00:39:06,744
We broke up.

525
00:39:07,578 --> 00:39:09,455
- It's time for you to accept it.
- No.

526
00:39:10,539 --> 00:39:13,959
I can't break up with you.
No, I'm not breaking up with you.

527
00:39:14,835 --> 00:39:16,628
I really loved you.

528
00:39:16,712 --> 00:39:18,213
Are you saying you didn't love me?

529
00:39:19,131 --> 00:39:20,257
Not even for a moment?

530
00:39:20,591 --> 00:39:22,092
I did have feelings for you.

531
00:39:22,676 --> 00:39:25,345
But it wasn't love.

532
00:39:25,429 --> 00:39:26,597
But why?

533
00:39:27,514 --> 00:39:29,141
What do I lack?

534
00:39:31,602 --> 00:39:33,437
It's not that you lacked anything.

535
00:39:33,729 --> 00:39:35,272
We just weren't right for each other.

536
00:39:35,773 --> 00:39:36,774
Cho-yi.

537
00:39:38,150 --> 00:39:41,445
You're perfect
just the way you are, okay?

538
00:39:46,283 --> 00:39:49,620
Do you know how much I struggled
and endured to put up with you?

539
00:39:50,370 --> 00:39:51,705
Are you saying
I wasn't right for you?

540
00:39:51,789 --> 00:39:54,333
Do you think all that struggling
and enduring means love?

541
00:39:56,043 --> 00:39:58,462
Someone who lets you be yourself.

542
00:39:59,797 --> 00:40:01,006
Find someone like that.

543
00:40:03,717 --> 00:40:05,093
This is ridiculous.

544
00:40:05,177 --> 00:40:07,513
You pretend to be polite and sweet.

545
00:40:08,347 --> 00:40:10,682
But you're just pretending
to be the better person to leave me.

546
00:40:11,934 --> 00:40:12,935
...I

547
00:40:14,186 --> 00:40:15,646
I won't ever break up with you.

548
00:40:16,897 --> 00:40:18,190
So...

549
00:40:19,566 --> 00:40:20,859
you might as well endure it.

550
00:41:00,148 --> 00:41:02,985
Well, should I play some music?

551
00:41:03,694 --> 00:41:05,028
Oh, yes. I'd love that.

552
00:41:10,075 --> 00:41:11,243
What...

553
00:41:13,245 --> 00:41:15,289
Why is this...

554
00:41:19,751 --> 00:41:20,752
INCOMING CALL
LEE CHAN

555
00:41:24,381 --> 00:41:25,632
ANSWER

556
00:41:26,174 --> 00:41:27,759
- Hello?
- <i>Where are you?</i>

557
00:41:28,635 --> 00:41:29,970
<i>It's really Chan.</i>

558
00:41:30,053 --> 00:41:32,014
I'm almost at work. Where are you?

559
00:41:32,347 --> 00:41:34,433
Me? Not sure.

560
00:41:35,434 --> 00:41:37,895
What? We spent all night together.
But do you miss me already?

561
00:41:38,645 --> 00:41:39,938
<i>"All night"?</i>

562
00:41:44,192 --> 00:41:46,403
Hey, stop joking around, will you?

563
00:41:46,486 --> 00:41:49,656
<i>What? We were good together
until this morning.</i>

564
00:41:50,032 --> 00:41:51,450
<i>Until this morning?</i>

565
00:41:51,533 --> 00:41:52,993
<i>By the way,
what am I supposed to pick up?</i>

566
00:41:53,076 --> 00:41:54,620
Whatever. I'll throw it out.

567
00:41:54,703 --> 00:41:55,913
You're better off without seeing it.

568
00:42:00,375 --> 00:42:03,962
<i>What can I do to show you how I feel?</i>

569
00:42:04,713 --> 00:42:06,673
<i>I love you, Chan.</i>

570
00:42:13,388 --> 00:42:16,725
<i>Is he throwing out that card?</i>

571
00:42:19,482 --> 00:42:21,067
<i>The power is off.</i>

572
00:42:59,230 --> 00:43:00,523
I can't believe

573
00:43:01,566 --> 00:43:03,484
Mr. Kang was in love with Chan.

574
00:43:07,989 --> 00:43:10,491
How did I end up
finding out this secret?

575
00:43:13,786 --> 00:43:14,787
You're still here?

576
00:43:45,902 --> 00:43:47,362
Director Lee.

577
00:43:47,445 --> 00:43:48,529
Have you been well?

578
00:43:51,366 --> 00:43:52,367
Yes.

579
00:43:55,662 --> 00:43:56,955
Oh, hello.

580
00:44:01,668 --> 00:44:04,671
Who was your favorite in D.N.X?

581
00:44:04,963 --> 00:44:06,214
Well...

582
00:44:07,131 --> 00:44:08,132
Pardon?

583
00:44:09,842 --> 00:44:11,177
How did you know that?

584
00:44:11,260 --> 00:44:13,304
You're listening to our song
from ten years ago.

585
00:44:20,979 --> 00:44:22,313
By any chance...

586
00:44:25,858 --> 00:44:26,985
was it me?

587
00:44:37,078 --> 00:44:38,079
Right?

588
00:44:40,581 --> 00:44:41,582
It was.

589
00:44:42,750 --> 00:44:43,960
<i>I'm doomed.</i>

590
00:44:44,043 --> 00:44:45,253
Gosh...

591
00:44:49,090 --> 00:44:52,176
How did you get that right
on your first try?

592
00:44:52,468 --> 00:44:54,762
Just my gut feeling.

593
00:44:58,016 --> 00:45:00,643
Oh, my gosh. That's crazy.

594
00:45:02,729 --> 00:45:04,939
You must've been a fan
since you were a kid.

595
00:45:06,399 --> 00:45:08,192
You can call me Chan
when it's just the two of us.

596
00:45:08,276 --> 00:45:09,986
Oh, no. Still...

597
00:45:10,361 --> 00:45:11,738
I will

598
00:45:13,197 --> 00:45:15,116
call you Da-reum.
Is that okay with you?

599
00:45:19,746 --> 00:45:20,747
Yes.

600
00:45:21,914 --> 00:45:23,082
Chan.

601
00:45:26,794 --> 00:45:29,839
It's been over ten years
since D.N.X disbanded.

602
00:45:29,922 --> 00:45:32,091
I didn't know there was still someone
who listened to our music.

603
00:45:32,842 --> 00:45:33,843
Thank you.

604
00:45:35,970 --> 00:45:39,057
I've listened to it for so long

605
00:45:39,140 --> 00:45:40,933
that it's become part of my routine.

606
00:45:41,309 --> 00:45:42,935
When I'm walking or working

607
00:45:44,270 --> 00:45:46,814
I find myself listening to it
without even realizing it.

608
00:45:48,024 --> 00:45:49,859
NAM DA-REUM

609
00:45:54,655 --> 00:45:56,449
- Give me your phone.
- What?

610
00:46:04,999 --> 00:46:06,959
I left it in the office.

611
00:46:45,581 --> 00:46:46,624
There.

612
00:46:53,673 --> 00:46:54,674
Call me.

613
00:46:58,427 --> 00:46:59,428
I will.

614
00:47:04,600 --> 00:47:05,685
You promise?

615
00:47:10,523 --> 00:47:12,108
No way.

616
00:47:12,900 --> 00:47:13,901
Awesome.

617
00:47:14,652 --> 00:47:16,863
Is this really Chan's number?

618
00:47:17,947 --> 00:47:18,948
Yes.

619
00:47:19,574 --> 00:47:22,076
Hey. Namda.

620
00:47:23,870 --> 00:47:25,246
She's completely out of it.

621
00:47:25,538 --> 00:47:27,081
A celeb giving you his number?

622
00:47:27,290 --> 00:47:28,583
What's that supposed to mean?

623
00:47:28,875 --> 00:47:31,085
He told you to call him.
Call him and find out.

624
00:47:32,920 --> 00:47:35,882
I doubt he really meant it.

625
00:47:35,965 --> 00:47:38,217
It's just that I work for his company

626
00:47:38,843 --> 00:47:40,344
and I'm an old fan, so...

627
00:47:40,428 --> 00:47:41,429
So?

628
00:47:43,931 --> 00:47:45,141
Oh, I don't know.

629
00:47:45,224 --> 00:47:48,477
Maybe he gave it to you
because he had a crush on you.

630
00:47:48,561 --> 00:47:50,354
- What?
- She's right.

631
00:47:50,688 --> 00:47:52,565
He could've saved your number
on his phone.

632
00:47:52,648 --> 00:47:54,358
Why did he have to do that?

633
00:47:54,442 --> 00:47:55,776
Why did he write it on your hand?

634
00:47:55,860 --> 00:47:57,028
He was totally flirting.

635
00:47:57,111 --> 00:48:00,615
Hey. He wasn't.
That's totally not true.

636
00:48:01,032 --> 00:48:02,033
First things first.

637
00:48:03,534 --> 00:48:04,535
Let's save it.

638
00:48:06,370 --> 00:48:07,580
Don't do anything other than saving.

639
00:48:15,671 --> 00:48:17,882
What the? Are you really calling him?

640
00:48:17,965 --> 00:48:19,300
Hey. No. Stop it.

641
00:48:19,383 --> 00:48:21,969
Are you nuts? Get back here.
Give it to me.

642
00:48:22,053 --> 00:48:23,221
Hey.

643
00:48:25,723 --> 00:48:28,184
What do I do? What am I going to say?

644
00:48:31,979 --> 00:48:33,272
Hello?

645
00:48:37,443 --> 00:48:39,070
Chan?

646
00:48:39,153 --> 00:48:41,948
It's me, Da-reum.

647
00:48:44,075 --> 00:48:45,284
<i>Hello?</i>

648
00:48:53,584 --> 00:48:55,962
Isn't this Director Lee's number?

649
00:48:56,379 --> 00:48:57,588
Director Lee?

650
00:48:58,631 --> 00:49:00,341
Yes, this is his number.

651
00:49:04,095 --> 00:49:08,808
I work for Director Lee's company.

652
00:49:08,891 --> 00:49:11,644
Oh, my Chan?

653
00:49:12,228 --> 00:49:13,562
He's in the shower.

654
00:49:19,777 --> 00:49:20,987
Sorry about that.

655
00:49:25,366 --> 00:49:28,077
Saying you work for him
after calling him Chan?

656
00:49:28,828 --> 00:49:29,829
That's beyond ridiculous.

657
00:49:29,912 --> 00:49:31,455
DELETE THIS CONTACT?

658
00:49:36,043 --> 00:49:37,295
BITTER SWEET

659
00:49:37,378 --> 00:49:38,546
What's the next scene?

660
00:49:38,629 --> 00:49:40,464
Prepare it thoroughly...

661
00:49:46,721 --> 00:49:48,222
What are you doing in my green room?

662
00:49:48,306 --> 00:49:49,432
The next scene.

663
00:49:50,099 --> 00:49:51,434
Will you help me rehearse?

664
00:49:53,394 --> 00:49:54,603
We still need to do our job.

665
00:49:54,687 --> 00:49:56,022
- Do you want to grab coffee?
- Let's get coffee.

666
00:50:04,613 --> 00:50:05,614
Namda.

667
00:50:08,868 --> 00:50:11,370
I told you not to call him. See?

668
00:50:11,454 --> 00:50:14,707
Why did he lead you on
when he has a girlfriend?

669
00:50:14,790 --> 00:50:16,292
I told you it wasn't like that.

670
00:50:16,584 --> 00:50:18,627
You're the same.

671
00:50:20,046 --> 00:50:22,298
Look what you've done.

672
00:50:22,798 --> 00:50:24,342
I'm doomed.

673
00:50:24,884 --> 00:50:27,053
Oh, I'm doomed.

674
00:50:27,345 --> 00:50:30,139
- It's your fault.
- Why did you do that?

675
00:50:30,222 --> 00:50:33,768
- You called him.
- Because you told me to.

676
00:50:35,144 --> 00:50:36,228
But you know what

677
00:50:37,688 --> 00:50:38,731
this is for the better.

678
00:50:39,440 --> 00:50:42,610
If Chan answered,
it would've been really awkward.

679
00:50:42,985 --> 00:50:44,070
Namda.

680
00:50:45,529 --> 00:50:46,530
You're not disappointed?

681
00:50:48,074 --> 00:50:51,035
Chan is human after all.
Of course, he can have a girlfriend.

682
00:50:51,285 --> 00:50:54,372
I actually want him to meet someone

683
00:50:54,955 --> 00:50:56,123
and be happy.

684
00:51:00,961 --> 00:51:04,423
Hey. A true fan is different.

685
00:51:04,799 --> 00:51:06,509
I approve.

686
00:51:08,844 --> 00:51:09,845
What time is it?

687
00:51:10,846 --> 00:51:12,098
Hey. It's time for Chan's drama.

688
00:51:12,181 --> 00:51:13,641
It's the first episode.
Make sure you stay for it.

689
00:51:32,201 --> 00:51:33,244
Hey.

690
00:51:35,329 --> 00:51:37,039
What's that look on your face?

691
00:51:37,748 --> 00:51:39,917
Are you out of your mind? Hey.

692
00:51:40,292 --> 00:51:42,420
Who are you to be disappointed?

693
00:51:42,503 --> 00:51:44,672
You've been a fan for 12 years.

694
00:51:44,755 --> 00:51:46,090
Get a grip.

695
00:51:56,725 --> 00:51:59,270
What if my call interrupted him?

696
00:52:00,187 --> 00:52:02,356
I hope
he doesn't think I'm a crazy fan.

697
00:52:04,358 --> 00:52:06,318
Oh, forget it.
I don't want to think about it.

698
00:52:21,167 --> 00:52:22,168
Hold on.

699
00:52:22,585 --> 00:52:24,712
<i>I love you, Chan.</i>

700
00:52:27,465 --> 00:52:29,216
If Chan has a girlfriend...

701
00:52:31,594 --> 00:52:32,845
what about Mr. Kang?

702
00:52:36,182 --> 00:52:38,350
Is it one-sided?

703
00:52:42,354 --> 00:52:44,773
That's pitiful.

704
00:52:47,234 --> 00:52:48,360
Oh, gosh.

705
00:53:04,627 --> 00:53:06,670
SUNGJU

706
00:53:26,315 --> 00:53:27,858
Here's your Americano.

707
00:53:29,860 --> 00:53:31,070
Thank you.

708
00:53:53,300 --> 00:53:55,970
<i>How long has he been bottling
his feelings alone?</i>

709
00:53:56,762 --> 00:53:57,930
<i>Did he want to stay by his side</i>

710
00:53:58,430 --> 00:54:00,057
<i>even as a friend?</i>

711
00:54:20,035 --> 00:54:22,413
Mr. Kang, have this

712
00:54:23,080 --> 00:54:24,248
and cheer up.

713
00:54:24,832 --> 00:54:25,833
Good luck.

714
00:54:39,013 --> 00:54:40,097
Mr. Kang.

715
00:54:41,348 --> 00:54:43,684
Mr. Kang. Were you looking for me?

716
00:54:45,227 --> 00:54:46,437
It's been up there for too long.

717
00:54:46,770 --> 00:54:48,230
I've seen it for too long,
it's not so impressive anymore.

718
00:54:49,648 --> 00:54:52,067
Okay, I'll replace it
as soon as possible.

719
00:54:55,613 --> 00:54:58,365
I thought you didn't drink coffee.
What's gotten into you?

720
00:54:59,700 --> 00:55:01,994
Well, it's not so bad.

721
00:55:05,664 --> 00:55:06,999
Good. One, two.

722
00:55:07,416 --> 00:55:09,835
Good. Look at the window. One, two.

723
00:55:09,918 --> 00:55:10,961
Nice.

724
00:55:11,045 --> 00:55:12,171
Fix his hair, please.

725
00:55:13,297 --> 00:55:15,591
Nice. One, two. Smile a bit.

726
00:55:15,674 --> 00:55:17,384
One, two. Excellent.

727
00:55:17,468 --> 00:55:18,927
One more. One, two.

728
00:55:19,303 --> 00:55:20,346
Good job.

729
00:55:21,805 --> 00:55:25,059
- I just love the photos today.
- The colors looked perfect.

730
00:55:26,393 --> 00:55:28,270
- Let me get ready for the next set.
- Okay.

731
00:55:29,313 --> 00:55:31,357
- Hey. Can I have my phone?
- Yes.

732
00:55:32,900 --> 00:55:34,568
- Did I get any calls?
- No.

733
00:55:35,486 --> 00:55:36,862
Are you expecting one?

734
00:55:38,072 --> 00:55:39,156
No.

735
00:55:39,239 --> 00:55:40,741
UNREAD

736
00:55:40,824 --> 00:55:42,409
I just wanted to treat her to a meal.

737
00:55:44,828 --> 00:55:46,830
- Who?
- Just...

738
00:55:48,499 --> 00:55:50,876
Someone I'm grateful to.

739
00:55:53,170 --> 00:55:57,257
Mr. Kang, please confirm the location
for the fashion show.

740
00:55:57,341 --> 00:55:58,342
Sure.

741
00:56:04,181 --> 00:56:06,016
Mr. Kang, do you drink coffee now?

742
00:56:08,811 --> 00:56:10,854
Yes, it happened somehow.

743
00:56:11,689 --> 00:56:13,607
- You may proceed.
- Thank you.

744
00:56:14,900 --> 00:56:15,984
Wait...

745
00:56:16,777 --> 00:56:17,820
Yes, sir.

746
00:56:18,821 --> 00:56:20,948
How is Nam Da-reum doing?

747
00:56:22,032 --> 00:56:23,534
In terms of work and all.

748
00:56:25,869 --> 00:56:27,079
I think

749
00:56:27,496 --> 00:56:28,997
she's very diligent.

750
00:56:29,081 --> 00:56:31,458
She always takes initiative
and does her best in everything.

751
00:56:32,209 --> 00:56:33,752
She's very cheerful.

752
00:56:36,880 --> 00:56:38,048
She actually asked me

753
00:56:38,132 --> 00:56:40,551
about how to become
the outstanding employee.

754
00:56:41,093 --> 00:56:42,261
The outstanding employee?

755
00:56:42,845 --> 00:56:43,846
Yes.

756
00:56:55,399 --> 00:56:57,359
- Are the materials ready?
- Yes.

757
00:56:57,693 --> 00:56:59,653
- Won-tae, let's go.
- Okay.

758
00:57:04,908 --> 00:57:07,619
Da-reum, have you sorted out
the messenger promotion message

759
00:57:07,703 --> 00:57:11,165
- on the Appello fashion show?
- Oh, yes.

760
00:57:11,248 --> 00:57:14,209
I prepared two reminder versions
for the day of the show.

761
00:57:14,293 --> 00:57:15,377
Give me one second.

762
00:57:26,555 --> 00:57:27,765
MESSENGER

763
00:57:29,016 --> 00:57:30,058
NO RESULTS FOUND

764
00:57:32,644 --> 00:57:34,480
- What's taking so long?
- I...

765
00:57:36,899 --> 00:57:38,358
The files are gone.

766
00:57:40,694 --> 00:57:41,820
Gone?

767
00:57:42,154 --> 00:57:43,238
Yes.

768
00:57:46,074 --> 00:57:47,159
I'll make them quickly.

769
00:57:47,242 --> 00:57:48,869
I've already done it once.
It won't take long.

770
00:57:49,244 --> 00:57:51,955
Did you actually do it?

771
00:57:58,921 --> 00:58:02,007
We're updating it tomorrow.
Make sure to send it to me by today.

772
00:58:04,009 --> 00:58:05,260
I'm sorry.

773
00:58:09,807 --> 00:58:13,060
<i>Did someone touch my computer?</i>

774
00:58:13,811 --> 00:58:16,021
<i>No, I doubt it.</i>

775
00:58:17,439 --> 00:58:18,816
<i>I probably lost it.</i>

776
00:58:31,620 --> 00:58:33,038
APPELLO FASHION SHOW
MESSENGER MESSAGE PROPOSAL

777
00:58:37,000 --> 00:58:38,961
I won't have a chance
of becoming an outstanding employee

778
00:58:39,753 --> 00:58:41,505
let alone an ordinary employee.

779
00:58:50,514 --> 00:58:52,891
How can he work overtime every day?

780
00:58:55,394 --> 00:58:57,396
Seriously, that's amazing.

781
00:59:10,409 --> 00:59:11,535
That's strange.

782
00:59:12,119 --> 00:59:15,330
I swear it was on the wallpaper.

783
00:59:20,794 --> 00:59:22,796
What? I'm just borrowing this.

784
00:59:23,755 --> 00:59:24,798
Okay.

785
00:59:38,186 --> 00:59:39,187
No.

786
00:59:39,730 --> 00:59:40,814
Oh, no.

787
00:59:42,733 --> 00:59:44,026
Don't overthink it.

788
00:59:51,325 --> 00:59:52,951
JANGSHINCHEON, GUDORIM

789
01:00:46,254 --> 01:00:49,091
INGUK STATION

790
01:00:50,801 --> 01:00:51,843
Mr. Kang.

791
01:00:52,552 --> 01:00:53,553
Don't you have an umbrella?

792
01:00:54,137 --> 01:00:55,973
What brings you here

793
01:00:56,056 --> 01:00:58,392
- I live around here.
- Really? Me too.

794
01:00:58,892 --> 01:01:00,477
Let's go. I'll walk you home.

795
01:01:00,560 --> 01:01:01,770
Oh, no. It's okay.

796
01:01:02,229 --> 01:01:04,106
- Then will you go on your own?
- What?

797
01:01:05,023 --> 01:01:06,024
No.

798
01:01:16,201 --> 01:01:18,412
What happened to your car?
Why did you take the subway?

799
01:01:19,037 --> 01:01:20,205
It's in the body shop.

800
01:01:22,290 --> 01:01:23,709
Did you work overtime today?

801
01:01:24,710 --> 01:01:25,877
Yes, a little.

802
01:01:27,754 --> 01:01:30,215
If you're getting home now,
it wasn't just a little overtime.

803
01:01:32,009 --> 01:01:33,552
Is there too much work to do?

804
01:01:33,635 --> 01:01:35,053
Oh, no.

805
01:01:35,804 --> 01:01:37,889
It's just that I made a mistake.

806
01:01:40,434 --> 01:01:44,813
I bet you never make any mistakes
because you're thorough.

807
01:01:45,105 --> 01:01:46,481
You're right. I don't.

808
01:01:49,443 --> 01:01:52,154
But I used to make a lot of mistakes
when I was a newbie.

809
01:01:53,655 --> 01:01:55,907
You make mistakes
because you're doing the job.

810
01:01:57,409 --> 01:01:58,744
If you don't do anything

811
01:01:59,369 --> 01:02:00,787
you won't make any mistakes.

812
01:02:02,039 --> 01:02:03,582
Don't be afraid and keep trying

813
01:02:04,583 --> 01:02:05,625
whether it's work

814
01:02:06,251 --> 01:02:07,252
or making mistakes.

815
01:02:10,964 --> 01:02:13,091
Thank you for saying that.

816
01:02:13,717 --> 01:02:15,135
I was actually discouraged until now.

817
01:02:17,137 --> 01:02:20,098
You're more caring than I thought.

818
01:02:21,349 --> 01:02:22,434
Than you thought?

819
01:02:23,101 --> 01:02:26,980
Yes, everyone is afraid of your glare
so they avoid talking to you.

820
01:02:27,355 --> 01:02:28,356
Didn't you know?

821
01:02:36,281 --> 01:02:37,532
What? Wait.

822
01:02:40,160 --> 01:02:41,703
Anyway, this is pretty cool.

823
01:02:41,995 --> 01:02:43,955
I didn't know
we lived in the same area.

824
01:02:44,915 --> 01:02:46,374
How come we haven't run
into each other until now?

825
01:02:54,132 --> 01:02:56,468
Bullying is the worst.

826
01:02:56,551 --> 01:02:58,303
Do you know how that feels?

827
01:03:00,639 --> 01:03:02,015
Maybe we have.

828
01:03:03,433 --> 01:03:04,434
At a neighborhood pub.

829
01:03:06,269 --> 01:03:07,270
What?

830
01:03:07,771 --> 01:03:09,064
If we ever have

831
01:03:10,232 --> 01:03:11,525
I bet it was
at a library or something.

832
01:03:12,067 --> 01:03:14,861
Because I don't go anywhere

833
01:03:14,945 --> 01:03:16,655
other than my house and the library.

834
01:03:17,489 --> 01:03:19,866
I didn't know we had a bar here.

835
01:03:19,950 --> 01:03:21,243
Why didn't I notice?

836
01:03:40,971 --> 01:03:42,639
<i>What happened that night...</i>

837
01:03:43,598 --> 01:03:45,642
<i>Right. I might as well bury it.</i>

838
01:03:47,227 --> 01:03:48,353
<i>Mr. Kang.</i>

839
01:03:48,854 --> 01:03:52,440
<i>I'll keep your secret to my grave.</i>

840
01:04:04,077 --> 01:04:06,454
That's my house right there.

841
01:04:06,538 --> 01:04:07,789
It's late. You should go home.

842
01:04:07,873 --> 01:04:09,249
But we're almost there.
Why would you...

843
01:04:09,583 --> 01:04:10,584
I'll walk you to your house.

844
01:04:10,667 --> 01:04:12,878
No, thank you for walking me home.

845
01:04:12,961 --> 01:04:15,672
You should go home. Thank you.

846
01:04:17,966 --> 01:04:19,217
It's slippery.

847
01:04:19,301 --> 01:04:20,760
- If you don't watch out...
- Mr. Kang!

848
01:05:02,761 --> 01:05:06,681
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

849
01:05:17,734 --> 01:05:20,362
EPILOGUE

850
01:06:30,181 --> 01:06:33,059
<i>This is the last train
bound for Gudorim.</i>

851
01:06:33,351 --> 01:06:38,064
<i>Passengers for Songdam
must board this train.</i>

852
01:06:38,857 --> 01:06:40,734
SUNGJU

853
01:06:40,817 --> 01:06:42,777
THIS TRAIN GUDORIM
NEXT TRAIN NONE

854
01:06:42,861 --> 01:06:44,738
GUDORIM

855
01:06:45,238 --> 01:06:46,906
INGUK STATION

856
01:06:55,373 --> 01:06:56,750
There's no chance she'd be here.

857
01:08:12,367 --> 01:08:13,368
{\an8}<i>What is this?</i>

858
01:08:15,412 --> 01:08:16,579
{\an8}<i>Our stage!</i>

859
01:08:17,205 --> 01:08:18,498
{\an8}<i>No!</i>

860
01:08:18,581 --> 01:08:20,041
{\an8}Let's cheer up just a bit more.

861
01:08:20,750 --> 01:08:22,043
{\an8}- Is she pretty?
- Jeez.

862
01:08:22,752 --> 01:08:24,754
{\an8}Was she too busy to call me?

863
01:08:25,797 --> 01:08:28,133
{\an8}Unless our information is sent to SE
in real time

864
01:08:28,216 --> 01:08:29,717
{\an8}- it's hard to find out.
- Taxi.

865
01:08:29,801 --> 01:08:30,885
{\an8}<i>Mr. Kang, you don't think</i>

866
01:08:31,594 --> 01:08:32,762
{\an8}the spy is...

867
01:08:33,304 --> 01:08:34,431
{\an8}<i>Ms. Nam.</i>

868
01:08:35,640 --> 01:08:36,766
{\an8}<i>As of this moment</i>

869
01:08:37,767 --> 01:08:38,852
{\an8}<i>you're fired.</i>

870
01:08:42,373 --> 01:08:44,375
{\an8}Subtitles by Eunsook Youn
and Songmi You

871
01:08:44,456 --> 01:08:46,458
